-- title:
--   Maximality of ξ_∞ and ξ₀ in the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^2\nmid M$, let $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ contain every unit that maps to $1$ under reduction $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$, and assume $M/p$ is nonzero in the relevant sense; let $hj$ record that the $q$-expansion $j(q)$, namely `jqModC ℚ`, lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the integral form ratios for $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$. Let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, i.e. a Deligne–Rapoport property bundle for the two-chart integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over $R_p$, comprising properness, flatness, integrality, local finite presentation and normality of the model, properness and relative-dimension-one smoothness at the auxiliary level `ΓN p M H hpM`, a curve model `Meta` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for the function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` together with an isomorphism `eeta` onto the base change, Galois equivariance of its points, normalisation of the chart coefficients, and smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, together with the remaining data of that structure. Let $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a valuation subring with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $\rho\colon R_p\to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structure map $R_p\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $O$ be a commutative local ring with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O\colon R_p\to O$ such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$, and let `toκ` $\colon O\to\kappa_A$ be a ring homomorphism with `toκ`$\circ\rho_O$ equal to the residue map composed with $\rho$. Write $X_O=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` for the pullback of the model along $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$, with structure morphism `XO.toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}O$, and let $\xi_\infty=$ `𝔛.ξinf A hA ρ hρ ρO toκ htoκ` and $\xi_0=$ `𝔛.ξzero …` be the two associated points of $X_O$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions: for every point $y$ of $X_O$ lying outside the preimage of the basic open $\{p\ne 0\}$ of $\operatorname{Spec}O$, if $y$ specialises to $\xi_\infty$ then $y=\xi_\infty$, and likewise if $y$ specialises to $\xi_0$ then $y=\xi_0$.
--
--   This records that the two branch points $\xi_\infty,\xi_0$ of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ are maximal points of that fibre: no point of the fibre properly generalises them. It is used in the analysis of the crossing points of the two branches, in particular by the statements on reading off chart coordinates near a branch and on the incomparability of branch ideals at a crossing point.
